Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: changelog entry for the Mach-O relocation fix

(cherry picked from commit a30c006246fc3c1588c5b1ed5083cd0e2aa1c917)
---
 changes/02-bugfix/1594-armv8a-macho-relocations.md | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 changes/02-bugfix/1594-armv8a-macho-relocations.md

diff --git a/changes/02-bugfix/1594-armv8a-macho-relocations.md b/changes/02-bugfix/1594-armv8a-macho-relocations.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..d3acf28c9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changes/02-bugfix/1594-armv8a-macho-relocations.md
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+- With `-system macosx`, armv8a programs that use global data now produce
+  assembly that Apple's assembler accepts: the `ADRP`/`ADD` pair is printed
+  with the Mach-O operators `@PAGE` and `@PAGEOFF` instead of the ELF syntax
+  ([PR #1594](https://github.com/jasmin-lang/jasmin/pull/1594);
+  fixes [#1593](https://github.com/jasmin-lang/jasmin/issues/1593)).
